  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "FROM HOPF ALGEBRAS TO TENSOR CATEGORIES — This is a survey on spherical Hopf algebras. We give criteria to decide when a Hopf algebra is spherical and collect examples.\n\n**FROM HOPF ALGEBRAS TO TENSOR CATEGORIES**\n\n*N. ANDRUSKIEWITSCH, I. ANGIONO, A. GARCÍA IGLESIAS*\n\n27 pp, 21 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** This is a survey on spherical Hopf algebras. We give criteria to decide when a Hopf algebra is spherical and collect examples. We discuss tilting modules as a mean to obtain a fusion subcategory of the non-degenerate quotient of the category of representations of a suitable Hopf algebra.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Introduction; 1 Preliminaries; 1.1 Notations; 1.2 Tensor categories; 1.4 Nichols algebras; 2 Spherical Hopf algebras; 2.2 Spherical Categories; 2.3 Quantum dimensions; 2.4 The non-degenerate quotient; 2.5 Pointed or copointed pivotal Hopf algebras; 2.6 Spherical Hopf algebras with involutory pi; 2.7 Ribbon Hopf algebras; 2.8 Cospherical Hopf algebras; 3 Tilting modules; 3.1 Quasi-hereditary algebras and tilting modu; 3.2 Induced and produced; 3.3 Finite-dimensional Nichols algebras of dia",
      "lang": "en",
